{"_id":"68a7360f8ec3d8323af131c9","nodeId":"DjTQjMbika4_yTzrBpcmB","roadmapSlug":"computer-science","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:54.940Z","description":"# CPU Cache\n\nA CPU cache is a hardware cache used by the central processing unit of a computer to reduce the average cost to access data from the main memory. A cache is a smaller, faster memory, located closer to a processor core, which stores copies of the data from frequently used main memory locations.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is CPU Cache","url":"https://www.howtogeek.com/854138/what-is-cpu-cache/","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3cf5"},{"type":"video","title":"MIT 6.004 L15: The Memory Hierarchy","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vjYF_fAZI5E&list=PLrRW1w6CGAcXbMtDFj205vALOGmiRc82-&index=24","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3cf6"},{"type":"video","title":"MIT 6.004 L16: Cache Issues","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajgC3-pyGlk&index=25&list=PLrRW1w6CGAcXbMtDFj205vALOGmiRc82-","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3cf7"},{"type":"feed","title":"Explore top posts about Computing","url":"https://app.daily.dev/tags/computing?ref=roadmapsh","_id":"6a7f4a1dcb44947debcf3cf8"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:21.077Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/computer-science/content/DjTQjMbika4_yTzrBpcmB.md"}